NAME
    type - print a file (the shell's built-in cat)

SYNOPSIS
    type path

DESCRIPTION
    Prints one file as it is, straight from the card: the shell's own
    cat, which needs nothing in /bin. type always runs the built-in
    (there is no /bin/type), while cat runs /bin/cat when it exists and
    this built-in only when it does not. Errors: "not found", "is a
    directory". Files of any size (up to 16M). type is a shell built-in.

LIMITS
    One file: no globs, no "-", no console input.

EXAMPLES
    type /README
    type /man/type

NOTES
    The shell's other stand-ins (dir, pwd, del, help) likewise answer
    only when /bin lacks the program, as on a freshly made card.
    New in Y1/OS 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    cat, more, dir
